# 2. STORY AND SETTING

### 2.1 The Story

The main character is a lazy factory employee who doesn't particularly enjoy working.

While everyone else is busy doing their jobs, our little employee is constantly looking for opportunities to avoid his responsibilities.

During lunchtime, he sneaks onto a factory conveyor belt.

What starts as an innocent attempt to have some fun turns into a ridiculous survival challenge when the factory machinery continues operating.

Now he must keep running in place and avoid the equipment travelling towards him.

The longer he survives, the more chaotic the factory becomes.

### 2.2 The Setting

The entire game takes place inside a colourful, cartoon-style factory.

The environment includes:
- Industrial machinery.
- Conveyor systems.
- Packaging equipment.
- Robotic arms.
- Storage areas.
- Factory equipment.
- Warning lights and safety signs.
- Different factory departments.

The factory should look playful and colourful rather than dark, dirty or realistic.

### 2.3 Humour and Personality

Humour should be part of the game's identity.

Examples of humorous messages:

| Situation | Message |
|---|---|
| Starting a game | "Back to avoiding work!" |
| Pausing | "Taking another break?" |
| Completing a level | "Congratulations! You avoided actual work." |
| Achieving a record | "Employee of the month? Absolutely not." |
| Game over | "You've been caught slacking!" |
| Restarting | "One more break!" |

The game should have funny character reactions, playful sound effects and occasional humorous factory announcements.

