# 13. TECHNICAL AND DEVELOPMENT PRINCIPLES

### 13.1 Platform

Initial development should prioritise Android mobile devices.

The game should be designed around touchscreen controls.

### 13.2 Performance

The game should:
- Run smoothly on supported mid-range devices.
- Have optimised 3D models.
- Use efficient obstacle spawning.
- Avoid unnecessary visual effects.
- Maintain responsive controls.
- Minimise loading times.

### 13.3 Game Architecture

The game should be designed with separate systems for:

1. Character movement.
2. Conveyor movement.
3. Obstacle spawning.
4. Obstacle behaviour.
5. Collision detection.
6. Difficulty progression.
7. Level management.
8. Endless survival management.
9. Scoring.
10. Rewards and customisation.
11. User interface.
12. Audio.

The two gameplay modes should share the same core movement and obstacle systems wherever possible.

Their progression and scoring rules should remain separate.

### 13.4 Gameplay Integrity

Obstacle generation must be tested to prevent impossible situations.

The game should not rely on random unfair obstacle placement.

Difficulty should be controlled through tested obstacle patterns, speed settings and reaction-time requirements.

